Package: togler
Version: __VERSION__
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 42), libglib2.0-bin
Maintainer: Caesar <https://github.com/caesar003>
Homepage: https://github.com/caesar003/togler
Description: Toggle application visibility on GNOME
 Togler is a command-line utility for toggling application window
 visibility on GNOME desktop environments. It provides a simple interface
 to show, hide, or launch applications with a single command.
 .
 Key features:
  * Toggle windows between visible and minimized states
  * Launch applications if not already running
  * Support for both Wayland and X11 sessions
  * Configurable WM_CLASS mappings for different applications
  * Bash completion support
 .
 Togler requires the companion GNOME Shell extension to be installed
 and enabled for full functionality.
